 "applies_to": "Strato OS537 thermostats running the 2-pipe / 4-pipe fan coil application of the universal firmware.",
 "summary": "In its fan coil application the OS537 drives on/off, floating or 0-10 V valves, a three-speed or ECM fan and an auxiliary output (reheat, occupancy, fan or network-controlled) over BACnet MS/TP. The object list has setpoints, mode, fan and occupancy commands, door, window, filter and service inputs, changeover and fan status, demands and two PID loops.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": "Universal firmware 1.2.6 and later",
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "The guide has no read/write column. Access here follows its tags: Cfg, User and Cmd objects are shown writable, Status objects read-only, and BO/AO objects commandable (the guide lists them for output overrides).",
  "AI-2 is printed in the I/O table without a row border and was read from the page text.",
  "AI-8 RoomCO2 exists only on C models such as the OS537MHC.",
  "BV-14 Aux_Cmd drives the auxiliary output when MSV-54 is set to Network.",
  "Multistate state numbers follow the order the states are printed, starting at 1; several MSVs print a range instead.",
  "MSV-48 prints 'COC/NH' for both changeover contact options; the second is described as normally cool."
 ],
